<h2>Agentic AI Innovations in Construction: (2) Resistance to disruption</h2>
<p> Despite the pressures catalogued in the first dimension, agentic AI faces two
reinforcing resistive forces that impede its penetration into established construction
workflows: (1) challenges to professional legitimacy and (2) concerns over project liability. 
</p>

<p>
<em>“AI agents are not going to disrupt the construction industry, imagine the
company replaced by non-physical items like ghosts, why [would] people use it, except
for capitalists? What tasks should I [delegate to my] junior staff or to my junior agents?”</em> Interview responses reported interconnected legitimacy concerns
in agentic AI systems. For example, the embodied on-site experience from the physical aspect is lacking in AI agents,
while epistemic risks, such as expert judgment accummulated through real-life experiences, worried the professionals,
especially on the social status and authority in socio-cultural settings.
</p>

